// quebec-law25 — Québec's Act respecting the protection of personal
// information in the private sector, as amended by Law 25
//
// The law: before communicating personal information outside Québec, an
// organisation must carry out a privacy impact assessment and may proceed
// only if the information would receive adequate protection (s. 17).
//
// This pack: everything runs in Québec, so no assessment is triggered.
// Offers must state their subdivision (`subdivision = qc`) to qualify.
//
// Not covered: transfers you have assessed and documented. If you rely on
// one, write your own policy instead of importing this one.
//
// Use `import "quebec-law25"`. Not legal advice.

policy quebec-law25 {
  residency = quebec
  min_trust = T2
}
